# BuildKit reads <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore in preference to a context-root
# .dockerignore. The context here is the directory holding all three repos, which
# is not itself a repo, so this is the only place the ignore list can be tracked.
#
# Without it `COPY ceynex-core/ .` drags in .venv/ (hundreds of MB), .git/, the
# raw data cache and the trained models — every one of which busts the layer
# cache on each rebuild.

**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/build
**/dist

# Rebuildable artefacts; the container gets these as volumes instead.
**/data/raw
**/data/staging
**/data/parquet
**/models
**/.cache
**/mlruns

# Local-only working files
**/.env
**/CLAUDE.md
**/CeyNex_plan_updated
**/CeyNex_plan.tar.gz

# The governing documents: ~15 MB of PDF and DOCX with no runtime role.
docs
**/docs/_text

# The frontend is deployed from its own VM, not baked into the API image.
**/web/node_modules
**/web/dist
